            <ArticleTitle>Progression of coronary disease in candidates for transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>497-500</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Five of our first 20 candidates for PTCA had unanticipated occlusion of the relevant coronary artery between the time of coronary angiography and PTCA. None had a change in symptoms or ECG to suggest coronary occlusion. We currently schedule PTCA within a month to help avoid this occurrence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
